course: dictionary
lesson: 10599
title: Context clues: undertaker
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An undertaker is a person whose job is to prepare a dead body for burial or cremation, and to arrange the funeral. Context helps you find this meaning. The sentence right after the word explains it: «"Funeral director" is the official name for an undertaker, the person who arranges funerals.»
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. Funerals, burials and cremations are all linked to the word, so an undertaker must be a person connected with them. Try it: «Businesses rename sad things to sound gentler: an undertaker becomes a "funeral director" and a cemetery becomes a "memorial park".» Does "funeral director" still make sense? Yes, so your meaning is right.
explain: Some words are chosen to sound gentler than the thing they name. Businesses use softer words for sad things, so «funeral director» is the polite modern word. Old stories and films sometimes show an undertaker as a spooky or comic character, but the word itself simply names a real job that helps families after someone dies.
fact: An undertaker prepares dead bodies for burial or cremation and arranges funerals.
fact: In the US, an undertaker is also called a funeral director or a mortician.
fact: «Funeral director» is the polite, modern word for an undertaker.
fact: «Memorial park» is a gentler name for a cemetery, which is a place where the dead are buried.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word, and they can give you clues to its meaning.
exercise: «"Funeral director" is the official name for an undertaker, the person who arranges funerals.» What is an undertaker? | A teacher of very young children | A person who sells cars | A person who guards a castle | *A person who prepares the dead for burial and arranges funerals
exercise: In the US, another name for an undertaker is: | Postman | *Mortician | Gardener | Lifeguard
exercise: «Businesses rename sad things to sound gentler: an undertaker becomes a "funeral director" and a cemetery becomes a "memorial park".» Which words are the gentler name for a cemetery? | gentler | *memorial park | undertaker | sad things
test: Which is the polite modern word for an undertaker? | *Funeral director | Coffin maker | Mortician | Gravedigger
test: Why do businesses use gentler words like «funeral director»? | Because the words mean something happy | *To sound softer about sad things | To make cemeteries bigger | To confuse their customers
exam: Read this: «An undertaker helps a family after someone dies.» What is the main job of an undertaker? | Running a gift shop | Painting pictures for the family | *Preparing the dead for burial or cremation and arranging the funeral | Cooking the meal after the funeral
